The long-format well join and heatmap are appropriate. The actual RLU range is 429–742, so your colour limits do not discard any observations. There is no obvious broad row/column gradient; occasional high-luminescence wells are consistent with active compounds.

The dataset has 192 compounds, with four test wells and four control wells per compound. Recomputing Welch’s tests and BH correction across all 192 compounds reproduces all four of your hits:

